    "title": "Measurement of the Decay $B^{-} \\to D^{*0} e^{-} \\bar{\\nu}_{e}$",
    "arxiv": "[0712.3493v1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0712.3493)",
    "time": "2007.12.20",
    "abstract": "Using 226 million $B\\bar{B}$ events recorded on the $\\Upsilon(4S)$ resonance with the BABAR detector at the SLAC $e^{+}e^{-}$ PEP-II storage rings, we reconstruct $B^{-} \\to D^{*0} e^{-} \\bar{\\nu}_{e}$ candidates in a partial data sample corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 232 fb$^{-1}$, where the $D^{*0}$ decays to $D^{0} \\pi^{0}$ with the $D^{0} \\to K^{-} \\pi^{+}$. We measure the branching fraction $\\mathcal{B}(B^{-} \\to D^{*0} e^{-} \\bar{\\nu}_{e}) = (5.56 \\pm 0.08 \\pm 0.41)\\%$ and the product of the form factor normalization and CKM matrix element $\\mathcal{F}(1) |V_{cb}| = (35.9 \\pm 0.6 \\pm 1.4) \\times 10^{-3}$.",
